## Recommended Batch 12 (Opus-direct, 2 items, ~55-60K combined)

### Item 1: Job Order Phase 2 (T2, ~35K)
Operationalizes the existing JobOrder router with field-service workflow primitives.
react-signature-canvas is already in package.json.

Files to touch (proposed scope — re-verify at pre-flight):
- apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/job-order.ts — extend with addPart, addServiceLine,
  recordSignature procedures. Parts and service lines are line-items on a JobOrder;
  signature is a base64 PNG stored on the JobOrder row.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/service/job-orders/[id]/page.tsx — add Parts
  + Services + Signature sections. Signature section shows captured signature image OR
  a "Capture signature" button when status=in_progress AND no signature yet.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/service/job-orders/[id]/signature-pad.tsx —
  NEW Client Component wrapping react-signature-canvas. On save: serializes to PNG
  base64 → calls trpc job-order recordSignature mutation → optimistic UI update.
- apps/web/src/__tests__/job-order.test.ts — extend with ~10 tests for the new
  procedures (parts/services CRUD + signature recording + status-gated mutations).
- packages/db/prisma/schema.prisma — add JobOrderPart + JobOrderServiceLine models if
  not already present; add signatureDataUrl text field to JobOrder if not present.
  Re-verify schema state at pre-flight grep before scoping migration.

### Item 2: Quotation UI inline edit for drafts (T2, ~25K)
Closes the last quotation builder UX gap. Currently editing a draft requires delete +
recreate; this adds in-place edit via existing quotationUpdate procedure.

Files to touch:
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/crm/quotations/[id]/edit/page.tsx — NEW
  Server Component, fetches quotation by id (only renders for status=draft), embeds
  <QuotationBuilder /> in edit mode with pre-loaded values.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/crm/quotations/new/quotation-builder.tsx —
  accept an optional `initialQuotation` prop. When present: pre-fill all form state +
  switch submit handler to call quotationUpdate instead of quotationCreate. Routes back
  to detail page on success.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/crm/quotations/[id]/quotation-actions.tsx —
  add "Edit draft" button gated on status=draft.
- apps/web/src/__tests__/crm.test.ts — extend with ~5 tests for quotationUpdate
  scenarios already covered at router level; UI integration is verified via typecheck.

